1
00:00:10,244 --> 00:00:13,569
-Do you --
Do you have a minute,
Mayor Mamdani?

2
00:00:13,569 --> 00:00:16,390
-Of course. But first, I need
to address this nor'easter.

3
00:00:16,390 --> 00:00:17,519
Quick, get out your phone.

4
00:00:17,519 --> 00:00:20,887
I need to send an urgent message
about this dangerous storm.

5
00:00:20,887 --> 00:00:22,714
-Ready, sir.

6
00:00:25,022 --> 00:00:26,552
Rain

7
00:00:26,552 --> 00:00:29,663
Avoid

8
00:00:29,663 --> 00:00:32,700
-Shelter in place, y'all. Mm.

9
00:00:33,382 --> 00:00:34,956
-Hey, uh, perfect.

10
00:00:34,956 --> 00:00:37,668
Now, Mr. Mayor,
there's someone here to see you.

11
00:00:37,668 --> 00:00:40,512
-What? What reckless lunatic
would travel to see me

12
00:00:40,512 --> 00:00:43,068
in this kind of weather?
That's crazy.

13
00:00:43,068 --> 00:00:46,425
-Your best friend.

14
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:50,338
Wonderful.

15
00:00:50,338 --> 00:00:53,698
- Oh, yes.
Mr. President,
you're here...again.

16
00:00:53,698 --> 00:00:57,645
-Of course I am.
I miss my Day One,
Zoran Mamdani.

17
00:00:57,645 --> 00:01:01,127
Of course, for some reason
that no one can figure out,

18
00:01:01,127 --> 00:01:03,285
I really, really like you.

19
00:01:03,285 --> 00:01:05,168
-That's -- That's very kind.

20
00:01:05,168 --> 00:01:08,698
But wouldn't you rather be
in DC?
We're in the middle of El Niño.

21
00:01:08,698 --> 00:01:10,993
-Oh, El Niño.
We don't like big storms,

22
00:01:10,993 --> 00:01:13,685
especially when they're
in Spanish.

23
00:01:13,685 --> 00:01:16,592
-Yeah, well, let's just pray
that it passes quickly.

24
00:01:16,592 --> 00:01:19,884
-Oh, I don't pray at all.
I don't go to church
on Christmas,

25
00:01:19,884 --> 00:01:22,346
&quot;nor'easter.&quot;
Boom!

26
00:01:22,346 --> 00:01:26,051
Somehow, when I'm with you,
I'm just firing
on all cylinders.

27
00:01:26,051 --> 00:01:28,271
Maybe it's
because we're both from Queens.

28
00:01:28,271 --> 00:01:31,182
-I know.
Isn't it funny to think
I could have grown up

29
00:01:31,182 --> 00:01:33,245
in one of your
apartment buildings in Queens?

30
00:01:33,245 --> 00:01:35,460
-Not with that last name.

31
00:01:36,036 --> 00:01:40,188
-Mr. President,
I'm actually very busy,
and I assume you are, too.

32
00:01:40,188 --> 00:01:45,757
-Wrong!
I just love hanging out
with you.

33
00:01:45,757 --> 00:01:48,308
We're like one of those
unlikely animal friendships,

34
00:01:48,308 --> 00:01:51,091
like when a tiger gets together
with a baby goat.

35
00:01:51,091 --> 00:01:54,410
When I see stuff like that,
I want to text it to you and say,

36
00:01:54,410 --> 00:01:56,976
&quot;This could be us,
but you playin'.&quot;

37
00:01:56,976 --> 00:02:00,188
Is that timely?
Do people still say that?

38
00:02:00,188 --> 00:02:01,627
Anyway, how are you?

39
00:02:01,627 --> 00:02:03,900
-I'm great.
It was a great summer.

40
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:07,338
I'm still riding high
on that Knicks championship.

41
00:02:09,227 --> 00:02:10,807
You know, I checked that out.

42
00:02:10,807 --> 00:02:14,601
I went to one game,
ruined the vibe,
and then dipped.

43
00:02:14,601 --> 00:02:18,623
-By the way, I took your advice
on Iran for my speech at the UN.

44
00:02:18,623 --> 00:02:22,175
Is it the &quot;U-N&quot; or &quot;un&quot;?
-&quot;U-N.&quot;

45
00:02:22,175 --> 00:02:25,886
Wait, so you said we need
to work towards a ceasefire
and sustain peace?

46
00:02:25,886 --> 00:02:30,038
-Oh, I could have sworn
you told me to say,
&quot;I'm going to annihilate you!&quot;

47
00:02:30,038 --> 00:02:33,493
-Yeah,
I don't think that was me.
-Maybe I dreamed it.

48
00:02:33,493 --> 00:02:38,334
You're in most of my dreams.
I call you &quot;Mam-dreamy.&quot;

49
00:02:38,334 --> 00:02:42,490
Pick me. Choose me. Love me.
Anyway...

50
00:02:42,490 --> 00:02:45,736
It's been a crazy week.
I kicked out the press

51
00:02:45,736 --> 00:02:49,365
and, uh, uh, hung out
with the president of China --

52
00:02:49,365 --> 00:02:52,095
Xi -- Xi.

53
00:02:52,095 --> 00:02:55,547
And, yeah, I went brunet.
It's fall.

54
00:02:56,072 --> 00:02:58,336
Mr. President, I-I-I just, um --

55
00:02:58,336 --> 00:03:00,384
-There was
this crazy AI stuff, too.

56
00:03:00,384 --> 00:03:04,620
I just had dinner
with Sam Altman, Elon Musk,
and Mark Zuckerberg.

57
00:03:04,620 --> 00:03:09,057
And it made me think, &quot;Wow,
RFK Jr.'s probably right
about those vaccines.&quot;

58
00:03:09,057 --> 00:03:11,094
I mean, the tizz in that room.

59
00:03:11,094 --> 00:03:14,265
You know what that's short for,
right -- the tizz?
Have you heard that?

60
00:03:14,265 --> 00:03:19,532
Maybe take a break from the AI
and start working
on &quot;A-eye contact,&quot; right?

61
00:03:19,532 --> 00:03:21,399
Some of these guys --
it's crazy.

62
00:03:21,399 --> 00:03:24,887
-Well,
that was a crazy thing to say,
but it's getting late.

63
00:03:24,887 --> 00:03:28,181
I have important work
tomorrow, okay?
I have to go to Bushwick

64
00:03:28,181 --> 00:03:31,884
and give ketamine
to underprivileged bisexuals.

65
00:03:31,884 --> 00:03:34,719
-I don't know what
any of those words mean.

66
00:03:34,719 --> 00:03:38,030
-Excuse me, Mr. President.
Someone is here to see you.

67
00:03:38,030 --> 00:03:42,529
-What reckless lunatic
would travel to see me
in this kind of weather?

68
00:03:42,529 --> 00:03:45,817
-It's your assistant,
Natalie Harp.

69
00:03:46,542 --> 00:03:48,761
-Hi.

70
00:03:53,487 --> 00:03:55,898
Hi, Mr. President. Hi.

71
00:03:55,898 --> 00:03:58,643
-Natalie, I didn't realize
you were in New York.

72
00:03:58,643 --> 00:04:03,913
-Oh, I wasn't.
I ran here from DC,
&quot;Weapons&quot;-style.

73
00:04:04,335 --> 00:04:08,059
-I, uh, came in case
you needed anything,
because, um...

74
00:04:08,059 --> 00:04:11,482
♪ Baby boy,
you've been on my mind ♪

75
00:04:11,482 --> 00:04:14,209
-Beyoncé.
Isn't she great?

76
00:04:14,209 --> 00:04:17,543
She's like the girl
from &quot;Obsession,&quot; but blonde.

77
00:04:18,726 --> 00:04:21,497
No.
No..

78
00:04:21,497 --> 00:04:25,834
No, I'm kidding,
I'm kidding, I'm kidding.
I'm totally normal.
I'm totally n-normal.

79
00:04:25,834 --> 00:04:29,841
Anyways, nice to meet you,
Mayor Mamdani.

80
00:04:29,841 --> 00:04:33,751
Excuse me. Excuse me.
I'm just going to
give him some...

81
00:04:33,751 --> 00:04:38,724
If you hurt him, I will end you.

82
00:04:38,724 --> 00:04:41,430
Okay, fine, fine!

83
00:04:41,430 --> 00:04:43,494
Wow.

84
00:04:43,494 --> 00:04:47,293
-Well, uh, Mr. President,
I really do
have to get back to work.

85
00:04:47,293 --> 00:04:49,461
-Oh, come on, Z-bag!

86
00:04:49,461 --> 00:04:51,751
ZZ Top.

87
00:04:51,751 --> 00:04:54,545
&quot;Zenon: The Zequel.&quot;

88
00:04:54,545 --> 00:04:56,725
Don't make me go back there.

89
00:04:56,725 --> 00:05:00,206
I don't want to go.
The judges keep telling me no.

90
00:05:00,206 --> 00:05:04,193
Mitch McConnell keeps
giving me the peace sign,
whatever the hell that means.

91
00:05:04,193 --> 00:05:08,205
Please let me stay here
with you.
-Okay.

92
00:05:08,205 --> 00:05:12,418
Only if you give us $21 billion
for a housing project in Queens.

93
00:05:12,418 --> 00:05:14,125
-Are you out of your mind?

94
00:05:14,125 --> 00:05:16,959
-What if I follow you back
on Instagram?

95
00:05:16,959 --> 00:05:17,916
-It's a done deal.

96
00:05:17,916 --> 00:05:22,199
-And live from New York,
it's &quot;Saturday Night&quot;!

97
00:07:26,068 --> 00:07:30,097
Musical

98
00:07:31,524 --> 00:07:35,496
Host

99
00:07:38,431 --> 00:07:43,368
-Ladies and gentlemen,
Jalen Brunson!

100
00:08:08,239 --> 00:08:12,270
Thank you. Thank you.

101
00:08:12,270 --> 00:08:14,825
Thank you very much.

102
00:08:14,825 --> 00:08:17,697
It's great to be here.
I'm very excited.

103
00:08:17,697 --> 00:08:21,262
You guys can probably tell
by my voice and face.

104
00:08:21,262 --> 00:08:25,274
But, tonight, I'm going to
approach hosting
the same way

105
00:08:25,274 --> 00:08:27,082
I approach a Knicks Finals game.

106
00:08:27,082 --> 00:08:31,329
So the first three quarters
of the show
are going to be godawful.

107
00:08:31,676 --> 00:08:35,404
The last sketch
is going to be amazing.

108
00:08:37,649 --> 00:08:40,510
Anyway -- Anyway,
I had a pretty good summer.

109
00:08:40,510 --> 00:08:43,420
I helped the Knicks
win the NBA championship.

110
00:08:46,076 --> 00:08:48,736
By now, you've all heard me
talk about it,

111
00:08:48,736 --> 00:08:51,723
but you haven't heard me
sing about it.

112
00:08:53,234 --> 00:08:56,190
And, obviously,
I'm not going to.

113
00:08:56,190 --> 00:08:59,325
But, look, the new season is
just a couple weeks away,

114
00:08:59,325 --> 00:09:03,182
and I got to say,
it's going to be pretty cool
to be back
in Madison Square Garden.

115
00:09:04,163 --> 00:09:08,252
Looking around like,
&quot;Wow, just a few months ago,

116
00:09:08,252 --> 00:09:12,331
this was the exact spot
where Taylor and Travis
got married.&quot;

117
00:09:12,331 --> 00:09:15,484
And I would say
the most satisfying part
of winning the title

118
00:09:15,484 --> 00:09:17,696
is thinking about all the people
who doubted me along the way.

119
00:09:17,696 --> 00:09:20,530
And tonight, I finally
get to get some closure.

120
00:09:20,530 --> 00:09:23,983
I invited one
of my biggest doubters here
to apologize to my face --

121
00:09:23,983 --> 00:09:26,101
Stephen A. Smith.

122
00:09:30,252 --> 00:09:34,060
You know what?
Let me say this,
Jalen Brunson.

123
00:09:34,060 --> 00:09:37,423
I am man enough
to admit that I was wrong

124
00:09:37,423 --> 00:09:40,383
when
the New York Knickerbockers
signed you,

125
00:09:40,383 --> 00:09:42,935
and I did not think
that you were the answer,

126
00:09:42,935 --> 00:09:46,825
nor did I believe that
you could deliver
the team's first championship

127
00:09:46,825 --> 00:09:50,638
since 1973,
when I was only 5 years old.

128
00:09:50,638 --> 00:09:54,572
-Sorry, Stephen. Uh,
how long is this going to go?
-About another seven minutes.

129
00:09:54,572 --> 00:09:55,392
-Yeah, forget it.

130
00:09:55,392 --> 00:09:57,644
-Okay. You got it.
-You're good.

131
00:09:59,473 --> 00:10:03,926
Now, before we start the show,
I did want to open it up
to some audience questions.

132
00:10:03,926 --> 00:10:06,425
Uh. Yes, to those four men
back there.

133
00:10:06,425 --> 00:10:08,947
-What's up, Jalen?
What's up, Jalen?

134
00:10:18,219 --> 00:10:21,539
What's up, big man?
Big fan. Big fan.

135
00:10:21,539 --> 00:10:25,077
Uh, bud, why -- why are you
wearing glasses inside?

136
00:10:25,077 --> 00:10:27,279
-You're right. You're right.

137
00:10:27,279 --> 00:10:29,038
Aye, aye, Captain.

138
00:10:29,038 --> 00:10:33,798
I have a question --
can you foul out of &quot;SNL&quot;?

139
00:10:33,798 --> 00:10:36,630
-No, I-I don't think so.

140
00:10:36,630 --> 00:10:40,989
-So I could be here, like,
the whole show.
Nice!

141
00:10:40,989 --> 00:10:43,384
-All right, who's next?

142
00:10:43,384 --> 00:10:44,538
Uh, Mikal.

143
00:10:44,538 --> 00:10:46,066
-Oh, I have a question.

144
00:10:46,066 --> 00:10:48,948
Are my arms, like, really long?

145
00:10:48,948 --> 00:10:51,087
They're pretty long, right?

146
00:10:51,568 --> 00:10:54,978
-Uh, yeah, buddy.
You got a
great wingspan.

147
00:10:54,978 --> 00:10:59,587
-Yet...I'll never fly.

148
00:11:01,007 --> 00:11:02,983
-Okay.

149
00:11:02,983 --> 00:11:06,296
Uh. Next question.
Uh, OG.

150
00:11:10,841 --> 00:11:16,215
-Remember in Game 4,
